#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Local visual oracle (MiniCPM-V). Cursor Agent stays on cloud Grok/Composer.
set -euo pipefail

base="${AI_BASE_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8093/v1}"
base="${base%/}"
model="${AI_MODEL:-minicpm-v-4.5}"
lan="http://nixos.local:8093/v1"

cat <<EOF
Cursor cannot keep cloud models (Grok / Composer / Claude) and a local
OpenAI endpoint in the same live picker. Override OpenAI Base URL is
global, and Cursor's backend cannot reach localhost without a public
HTTPS tunnel.

Visuals (all local clients): MiniCPM-V 4.5 on the R9700.
  • endpoint  ${base}  (model ${model})
  • LAN       ${lan}
  • capture   vl-capture.py (Advait tools/agent) — do not paste PNGs into cloud seats

Coding stays off this GPU:
  • Cursor Agent / CLI  → cloud Grok (Hard) / Composer 2.5 high (default)
  • Pi default chat     → /model opencode/nemotron-3-ultra-free (high)
  • visuals in Pi       → /model minicpm-v-4.5
  • longctx              → parked (MiniCPM5-2B too slow)
  • Continue / Zed / Hermes / Grok TUI local picker → ${model}

hipfire 27B is parked (Conflicts with minicpm-v.service). Do not start it
while MiniCPM-V is resident.

Health:
  curl -s ${base}/models | jq '.data[].id'
  curl -s ${lan}/models | jq '.data[].id'   # LAN (other machines)
EOF

if curl -fsS --max-time 2 "${base}/models" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo
  echo "Local VL server: UP (${base})"
else
  echo
  echo "Local VL server: DOWN (${base})" >&2
  exit 1
fi
